.env
.env.*
!.env.example
# Service-account JSON / API keys / GEE credentials — NEVER commit
secrets/
secrets/*
*.pem
*-credentials.json
*-service-account.json
# Host-bridge capability tokens — live secrets. Use capabilities.example.json as template.
host_bridge/capabilities.json
host_bridge/capabilities.json.bak.*
# ── workspace/ is the gateway's RUNTIME data directory — ignored wholesale ──
# Regenerable/replicated (Q17.1 warm-spare rsync + §56 per-KB source-ledgers +
# DR tarballs); NOT source-of-truth in git. Tracking live-mutated state
# perpetually-dirtied the working tree, blocking `git checkout main` +
# `git pull --ff-only` on the host and keeping the auto-deploy poller inert.
# The ONLY tracked workspace/ files are hand-authored SEEDS a fresh clone needs;
# they're committed explicitly (`git add -f`) and tracking wins over this ignore:
#   migrations/  projects/  prompts/**/v001.md  skills/
#   + config seeds: mcp_servers.json delegation_settings.json
#     meta_agent_settings.json llm_catalog_overrides.json adversarial_tasks.json
workspace/
# Raw eval-harness run output (evals/run_eval.py --out) — reproducible on
# demand, not a curated artifact. Record a summary in docs/PROGRAM.md
# instead of committing the JSON if a result is worth keeping permanently.
evals/results/
# Scorer output is regenerated from a (gitignored) results file by
# `python evals/score.py <report>` — tracking it would leave stale verdicts in
# the repo. The human-facing review sheets (evals/review/*.md) stay tracked.
evals/review/*.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
*.egg-info/
dist/
.venv/
*.log
.DS_Store
*.pem
*.key
*.p12
*.pfx
firebase-service-account.json
# Host Bridge — capability tokens contain secrets
host_bridge/capabilities.json

# Wiki lock files (transient)
wiki/.locks/*.lock
# Compiled CoreLocation helper binary
signal/location-helper
wiki/.slides/

# (Former workspace/ runtime + §55 + 2026-06-18 patchwork rules removed —
#  all subsumed by the single `workspace/` wholesale ignore above.)

# 2026-06-20: gateway-written wiki runtime (self-reflection digests, hot topics,
# privacy audit) — same untrack rationale as workspace/ (#167/#170): continuously
# rewritten, dirtied the tree + blocked deploy_gateway.sh git pull --ff-only.
# Hand-authored wiki pages (meta/, index.md, project pages, .obsidian) stay tracked.
wiki/hot.md
wiki/privacy/
wiki/self/
